# What Vercel does not need.
#
# The project's Root Directory is `app`, so only the Next.js client is ever
# built. But the CLI uploads from the repository root, and this repository also
# holds a Rust workspace: `target` alone is hundreds of megabytes, and the
# upload is capped at 15,000 files. Without this, `vercel --prod` fails before
# it starts with 41,473 files.
#
# The Git integration does not need this file, since it clones and honours
# .gitignore. It is here so a manual deploy behaves the same way.

target
node_modules
.git

# The program, the engine, and everything that only exists to build or test
# them. None of it reaches the browser.
programs
crates
tests
tools
phase0-private-counter
Cargo.toml
Cargo.lock
Anchor.toml

# Long-form documentation. Read on GitHub, not served by the app.
docs
